{"phases":32,"frame":"Pelvis frame, units = leg length (thigh+shin = 1). Origin = mid-hip. +x = skier's RIGHT (left hip -> right hip), +y = up the spine (mid-hip -> mid-shoulder, orthogonalised to x), +z = x cross y = BACKWARD (forward = -z). The cycle is ONE RIGHT TURN: phase 0 = edge change into the right turn, ~0.5 = apex, phase 1 = next edge change. Play the next (left) turn by mirroring: x -> -x and swap l_/r_; negate inclination, twist, feetYaw, hipLateral. The pair is periodic and Fourier-smoothed, so phase 31 -> mirrored phase 0 is continuous.","inclination":[0.0286,0.1143,0.2,0.2845,0.3669,0.4459,0.5204,0.5894,0.652,0.7072,0.7546,0.7934,0.8235,0.8447,0.8571,0.8607,0.8561,0.8434,0.8233,0.796,0.7622,0.7222,0.6764,0.6252,0.5689,0.5077,0.4419,0.3718,0.2978,0.2201,0.1394,0.0563],"inclination_note":"radians, lean of the line mid-ankle -> mid-hip from gravity vertical, sideways relative to the pelvis; + = hips to the skier's right of the feet (inside of a right turn)","hipHeight":[0.6146,0.6351,0.6527,0.6667,0.6763,0.6809,0.6801,0.6739,0.6625,0.6462,0.6258,0.6023,0.5768,0.5504,0.5244,0.4998,0.4777,0.4589,0.444,0.4335,0.4275,0.4261,0.4292,0.4365,0.4476,0.4622,0.4797,0.4998,0.5217,0.5449,0.5686,0.5921],"hipHeight_note":"vertical height of mid-hip above mid-ankle / leg length (1 = standing straight over the feet)","hipLateral":[0.0249,0.0836,0.1449,0.2077,0.2702,0.331,0.3882,0.4401,0.4854,0.5227,0.5513,0.5707,0.5808,0.582,0.5752,0.5613,0.5416,0.5175,0.4902,0.4609,0.4306,0.4001,0.3695,0.339,0.3083,0.2768,0.2438,0.2084,0.1699,0.1276,0.0811,0.0302],"hipFore":[-0.125,-0.142,-0.1545,-0.1611,-0.161,-0.1549,-0.1444,-0.1317,-0.1197,-0.111,-0.1076,-0.111,-0.1213,-0.1376,-0.1578,-0.1792,-0.1989,-0.2137,-0.2215,-0.2206,-0.2108,-0.1931,-0.1695,-0.1428,-0.1163,-0.0932,-0.0762,-0.0671,-0.0667,-0.0742,-0.0882,-0.1061],"hipOffset_note":"horizontal offset of mid-hip from mid-ankle / leg length: lateral (+ = right) and fore (+ = forward)","twist":[0.2133,0.3222,0.4195,0.5016,0.5659,0.